<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Chopin is a 28-year-old pianist in the fourth week of the continuation phase of rifapentine, moxifloxacin, and isoniazid for cavitary pulmonary tuberculosis, given by video-observed therapy. Three days ago he developed a scratchy throat and a runny, blocked nose, then a mild dry cough; two of his students had colds last week. His temperature at home has been up to 37.7 °C. He is frightened that the tuberculosis is coming back, because the cough is the first he has had in a month. He has no blood in his sputum, no night sweats, and no weight loss; he has gained 1.6 kg since the end of the intensive phase. He has taken every dose on his video calls. He has not taken anything for the cold yet and asked whether zinc lozenges or an antibiotic would help. He has no tendon pain, tingling, rash, yellowing, or dark urine. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Throat and nose, with a mild cough</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Scratchy throat, runny and blocked nose, dry cough</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Mild; teaching with difficulty</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Week 12 of 17 of tuberculosis treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Students with colds last week</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Nothing taken yet; no doses missed</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Temperature up to 37.7 °C; no hemoptysis, night sweats, or weight loss</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

